      note "Filing the motion extends the responsive-pleading deadline to 14 days after the court denies or postpones disposition (Rule 12(a)(4)(A))."
    }
    duration { min 3.1.days, mode 10.5.days, max 21.days }
    note "This pack doesn't separately model which Rule 12(b) defenses a motion raises, so sets waived-12h-defenses on every 12(b) motion as the conservative default: FRCP 12(h)(1)(A) waives lack of personal jurisdiction, improper venue, insufficient process, and insufficient service of process by omitting any of them from a motion made under the circumstances described in Rule 12(g)(2) (a motion raising some, but not all, available Rule 12 defenses). A pack that modeled motion content in more detail could instead set this flag only on the omitting variant."
    sets [waived-12h-defenses]
  }
  edge-removed-response-window-default-entered "Fail to answer or move -- default exposure" -> default-entered {
    authority cite "FRCP 55(a)"
    effort 0.hours
    valence bad
