decision joinder-decision: "Joinder of Parties" by applicant cite "FRCP 19; 20; 24"
{
  group amendment-joinder-group
  note "Rule 19 requires joinder of a party whose absence would prevent complete relief, impair that party's ability to protect its interest, or expose an existing party to a substantial risk of multiple or inconsistent obligations -- if joinder is not feasible (e.g., destroys diversity), the court weighs Rule 19(b) factors to decide whether the action can proceed 'in equity and good conscience.' Rule 20 permits joinder of parties whose claims/defenses arise from the same transaction and share a common question. Rule 24 lets a nonparty intervene as of right (an unprotected interest relating to the property/transaction) or permissively (a common claim/defense and no undue delay/prejudice)."
  court_listener_url "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/107609/provident-tradesmens-bank-trust-co-v-patterson/"
  joinder-required-or-permissive "Join a required party (Rule 19) or a permissive party (Rule 20)" -> parties-joined {
    authority cite "FRCP 19(a); 20(a)"
    effort 8.hours
    cost 2_500.usd
  }
  joinder-intervention "Nonparty intervenes as of right or permissively" -> parties-joined {
    authority cite "FRCP 24(a); 24(b)"
    effort 8.hours
    cost 2_500.usd
  }
  edge-joinder-decision-rule26f-conference "No joinder -- proceed to discovery planning" -> rule26f-conference {
