state rule26f-conference: "Rule 26(f) Conference" by applicant cite "FRCP 26(f); 26(d)(1)"
{
  group discovery-group
  note "THE DISCOVERY MORATORIUM: Rule 26(d)(1) bars seeking discovery 'from any source' before the parties confer under Rule 26(f), absent a Rule 26(a)(1)(B) exemption, stipulation, or court order -- no one has to wait for opposing counsel to propose the conference, since 26(f)(1) makes both sides' attorneys jointly responsible for arranging it. The conference must occur as soon as practicable, and in any event at least 21 days before a scheduling conference is held or a Rule 16(b) scheduling order is due."
  edge-rule26f-conference-initial-disclosures "Conduct Rule 26(f) conference and submit discovery plan" -> initial-disclosures {
